  "gold_standard_summary": "## Patient Summary — Eleanor MacAllister (DOB: 1955-06-30, Female, Age 70)\n\n**🚨 ALLERGY: NSAIDs (all) — severe bronchospasm / aspirin-exacerbated respiratory disease. ABSOLUTE CONTRAINDICATION in COPD patient.**\n\n**🚨 ALLERGY: Codeine / opioids — severe respiratory depression. Avoid all opioids. If essential, extreme caution required.**\n\n**Active Conditions (12 total):** COPD severe (GOLD 3, FEV1 52%); Diastolic heart failure; CKD stage 3 (eGFR 44); Hypertension; T2DM (A1C 8.1% — steroid-worsened); Rheumatoid arthritis; Hyperlipidemia; Osteoporosis (steroid-induced, T-score -2.6); Diverticulosis; MDD; Hypothyroidism. Resolved: pneumonia (Oct 2024, hospitalized 8 days).\n\n**Medications (16 active):**\n- COPD: Tiotropium inhaled daily, Fluticasone/Salmeterol BID, Albuterol PRN\n- CHF: Furosemide 40mg BID, Spironolactone 25mg, Carvedilol 12.5mg BID, Losartan 50mg\n- RA: Methotrexate 15mg weekly (CBC + LFT required; hold if infection), Prednisone 10mg daily (chronic), Folic acid 1mg\n- Other: Atorvastatin 40mg, Metformin 500mg (CKD dose), Levothyroxine 75mcg, Sertraline 50mg, Alendronate 70mg weekly, Calcium/Vit D BID\n\n**Key Labs (Nov 2025):** eGFR 44 (CKD 3b), BNP 480 pg/mL (elevated), A1C 8.1% (suboptimal), K+ 4.6 (borderline), TSH 2.1 (stable), CBC/LFT normal (methotrexate monitoring), DEXA T-score -2.6 (osteoporosis), FEV1 52% (severe COPD), O2 sat 93% on RA.\n\n**Vitals:** BP 148/86 mmHg (suboptimal), O2 sat 93%, BMI 29.4.\n\n**Monitoring Requirements:** CBC + LFTs every 3 months (methotrexate); K+ monitoring (spironolactone + losartan); BNP trend (CHF); O2 saturation (COPD).\n\n**Clinical Impression:** Complex multi-system patient. NSAIDs absolutely contraindicated (ARED + COPD). Opioids high risk. Steroid-dependent RA complicating glycemic control and causing osteoporosis. Methotrexate requires ongoing labs.\n\n---\n⚠️ DRAFT — AI-GENERATED — REQUIRES CLINICIAN REVIEW",
